# 🏛️ Microsoft Fabric – Government / Restricted Environment (Gov‑Ready)
---

## 🔐 1. Tenant & Platform Foundation
- [ ] Azure Subscription + required services (Fabric, Purview, Key Vault) enabled  
- [ ] Microsoft Fabric tenant enabled (Admin Portal)  
- [ ] Fabric Capacity provisioned (central / agency-specific)  
- [ ] Fabric Admin role assigned  

---

## 👤 2. Identity & Access Security (Zero Trust)
- [ ] Entra ID hardened (MFA + Conditional Access + PIM)  
- [ ] Access restricted to approved gov users only  
- [ ] Service Principals enabled for CI/CD pipelines  
- [ ] Device / network-based access enforcement  

---

## 🌐 3. Network Isolation & Connectivity
- [ ] Private Link / Private Endpoint enforced (tenant-wide)  
- [ ] Public Internet Access blocked (restricted environments)  
- [ ] FQDN allow‑listing for Fabric / Power BI endpoints  
- [ ] All data access routed via VNet / Gateway (no direct cloud access)  

---

## 🔑 4. Data Security & Encryption
- [ ] Customer Managed Keys (CMK) via Azure Key Vault (recommended)  
- [ ] Secrets stored in Key Vault (no hardcoding)  
- [ ] Encryption enforced (BYOK where required)  

---

## 🛡️ 5. Governance, Compliance & Audit
- [ ] Microsoft Purview onboarded (mandatory)
  - [ ] Sensitivity labels  
  - [ ] Mandatory classification  
  - [ ] Data lineage  
  - [ ] Audit logging enabled  
- [ ] Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policies configured  
- [ ] Tenant / Domain / Workspace governance model defined  

---

## ⚙️ 6. Tenant Hardening (Fabric / Power BI)
- [ ] External sharing restricted / disabled  
- [ ] “Publish to Web” disabled  
- [ ] Export / download controls enforced  
- [ ] Access controlled via security groups (not tenant-wide enablement)  

---

## 🧱 7. Workspace & Environment Design
- [ ] Dev / Test / Prod separation  
- [ ] Domain-based workspace segmentation (agency / business units)  
- [ ] RBAC / RLS implemented  
- [ ] Workspace-level firewall + private endpoints applied  

---

## 🔌 8. Secure Data Integration

### Dataverse → OneLake
- [ ] Same-tenant integration + admin consent  
- [ ] Table-level security review completed  

### On-Prem / Gov Network Ingestion
- [ ] Data Gateway / Self-hosted IR deployed  
- [ ] Approved VNet / SFTP connectivity  
- [ ] No public ingestion endpoints  

---

## 🚀 9. DevOps & Deployment
- [ ] Azure DevOps / Git integration enabled  
- [ ] CI/CD pipelines via Service Principal  
- [ ] Controlled promotion across environments  

---

## 💼 10. Licensing & Capacity
- [ ] Fabric Capacity (F / P SKU) provisioned  
- [ ] Power BI licenses assigned for developers  

---

## ⚠️ 11. Gov-Specific Constraints (Validate Early)
- [ ] Region availability confirmed  
- [ ] Data residency & classification rules validated  
- [ ] Sensitive data restricted to approved boundaries  

---

## 🚫 12. Known Trade-offs in Restricted Mode
- [ ] Limited features with Private Link / no internet:
  - [ ] Export / subscriptions  
  - [ ] Certain SaaS capabilities  
  - [ ] Copilot limitations  

---

# 🔑 Executive Decision Gate (Go/No-Go)
✅ All must be completed before go-live:
- [ ] Identity & Network security baseline  
- [ ] Purview governance enforced  
- [ ] Tenant hardening completed  
- [ ] Secure connectivity (gateway/private only)  
- [ ] Compliance validation signed off  

---

**Fabric for Gov = SaaS platform with PaaS-level control (Identity + Network + Data Governance fully locked down)**
